  "footnotes": [],
  "issues": [
    "No prices appear anywhere in the sheet; every priceUsd is null. The only numbers are volumes (SU 330 ml. / 750 ml.), V60, 3. NESIL and liquor labels (NO:7, NO:10, 12 Y.O.).",
    "Menu title row (CAFE VERDE PREMIUM) is not part of the JSON shape and was dropped.",
    "Herbal tea list (TAZE DEMLEME BITKI CAYLARI) has HIBISKUS / HIBISCUS here; the Tea Lounge sheet has BAMYA CICEGI / OKRA FLOWER. The sheet also lacks the FRESH MEYVE SUYU item present in Tea Lounge.",
    "MESRUBATLAR / SOFT DRINKS is followed, without a heading, by TAZE DEMLEME BITKI CAYLARI, 3. NESIL KAHVELER and the Ronnefeldt rows; the hot items are kept in document order inside MESRUBATLAR (they have detail lines so they were read as items, not headings).",
    "RONNEFELDT BITKI CAYLARI / RONNEFELDT HERBAL TEAS is immediately followed by RONNEFELDT POSET CAYLAR with no products between: read as a parent heading with two sub-categories (POSET CAYLAR, TAZE DEMLEME CAYLAR). The heading hierarchy is a guess.",
    "3. NESIL KAHVELER / THIRD GENERATION COFFEES has one line 'CHEMEX , V60 , SYPHON' (not bilingual): put in both detailTr and detailEn; could instead be a heading with three items.",
    "'SU / WATER 330 ml.' and '750 ml.': split literally into tr 'SU' / en 'WATER 330 ml.' (the volume only ends up in the English half).",
    "BRITVIC detail 'TOMATO, BITTER LEMON, GINGER ALE, TONIC' is printed once (English only): placed in detailEn, detailTr null.",
    "Ronnefeldt tea bags: after ENGLISH BREAKFAST the line 'SIYAH CAY / BLACK TEA' was read as its detail, while 'NANE & PEPPERMINT', 'PAPATYA / CAMOMILE' and 'ROOIBOS VANILYA / ROOIBOS VANILLA' were read as separate items with no detail. The pairing in this block is ambiguous (e.g. 'PAPATYA / CAMOMILE' could be the detail of NANE & PEPPERMINT).",
    "AYURVEDA HERBS & GINGER: English ingredients run over two spreadsheet rows; joined with a space into one detailEn.",
    "MILKSHAKES has two Turkish/English row pairs (description, then flavour list); each pair is joined with a newline inside detailTr / detailEn.",
    "COLD BREW has only one detail line, 'SOGUK DEMLEME ESPRESSO' (Turkish only): detailTr set, detailEn null.",
    "ROYAL DONDURMA / ROYAL ICE CREAM is followed only by flavour lists: kept as its own category with one item of the same name carrying the flavour lists as details. Could instead be an item in the iced tea category.",
    "JASMINE PEARLS has a detail identical to MORGENTAU (mango/bergamot green tea with sunflower, rose, cornflower): likely copy-paste in the source; kept as printed.",
    "English detail of GET THE POWER (musk mallow, cola plant, blackcurrant...) does not match the Turkish one word for word (AMBER CICEGI...); kept as printed.",
    "'TGPOF*' on EARL GREY has an asterisk but no footnote is printed on the sheet.",
    "Source typos kept verbatim, e.g. HUCCKLEBERRY FRIEND, COCOA SELL, LEMON PEE, CHEERY MANIA, MELON,MANDARIN.",
    "Alcohol sections (BIRALAR to IRLANDA VISKILERI) are brand names only: tr and en identical, no details, no prices, no serving sizes.",
    "IMZA KOKTEYLLER: ingredient lines are Turkish only (detailTr set, detailEn null). ULUSLARARASI KOKTEYLLER (INTERNATIONALS COCKTAILS as printed): ingredient lines are English only (detailEn set, detailTr null). Each name is followed by exactly one comma-separated line, read as its detail.",
    "Source typos kept verbatim in liquor/cocktail rows: HIBUSKUS EKSISI, NENE YAPRAKLARI, ANGUSTRA BITTER, MILAGRA REPOSADO, GRANDE ABSENTH, BOOLS ELDER FLOWER, BATI DE COCO, FRESH LEMON&ORANGE JUICE, MARIGOLD FLOWERI."
  ]
